# Q1 — OPENCODE_API_KEY from env; AGENCY_MODEL listed by `opencode models`
Date: 2026-10-13. Container: agency-base:2.0.26 as agency-spike-q (dummy invalid key in env only, never in a file).

## Commands + trimmed output

$ docker exec agency-spike-q opencode models
Error: Server process exited with code 1
PlatformError: Unknown: FileSystem.writeFile (/etc/agency/service.json.tmp)
  [cause]: Error: EROFS: read-only file system, open '/etc/agency/service.json.tmp'
    at cli.server-connection.resolve (...)

$ docker exec agency-spike-q opencode models --standalone
(rc=0, no output — empty model list)

$ docker exec agency-spike-q sh -c 'echo AGENCY_MODEL=${AGENCY_MODEL:-<unset>}'
AGENCY_MODEL=<unset>

Server log (all spike containers, dummy key):
  level=WARN message="failed to load OpenCode provider config"
    cause="OpencodeConsole.SignedOut: Reconnect OpenCode Console to continue."
Session prompt with dummy key (see q08.log) resolved model
  {"id":"cat-jam-free","providerID":"opencode"} then failed with provider.auth.

## Observation
- Serve DOES pick up OPENCODE_API_KEY from the environment: with a dummy
  value the provider attempted authentication and the Console refused it
  (provider.auth/401), not a missing-variable error.
- `opencode models` without a valid key lists nothing (empty output with
  --standalone). The plain form additionally needs a writable config dir
  for service registration (EROFS on the read-only /etc/agency mount).
- AGENCY_MODEL is unset in this environment, so "is the id listed" cannot
  even be attempted.

## Verdict: NOT PERFORMED (no provider key; AGENCY_MODEL unset)
